paper/sections/A_appendix.tex:254:\caption{Budget-matched negative controls (\textbf{v0/v3-era numbers, pre-v6}; included as historical record of disqualified designs and \emph{not comparable} with the v6 ensemble numbers in Table~\ref{tab:main_results}). The v0 Direct / SubspaceAD fusion / AnomalyClaw rows in this table use our older v0 descriptor Direct and our v3 router \texttt{AnomalyClaw} system; the main-paper headline numbers (GPT-5.4 $0.864$, SeedVL $0.809$, Qwen3.5 $0.814$) are from the v6 agent$+$Direct ensemble on the same test split. ``Random escalation'' and ``DINOv2 blend'' are calibration-split numbers for disqualified designs. This table's purpose is only to show that blind second-call escalation and weaker expert blends are negative controls; it should not be read as a competing test-split comparison against our headline v6 recipe.}
